# SyncVete brand (UI V2)

Full token reference: `docs/ui-v2/BRAND.md`. PR checklist: `docs/ui-v2/PR-CHECKLIST.md`.

## Must

- Keep SyncVete teal as the product default (`DEFAULT_THEME.accent = 'teal'`, `--clinic` / `--sv-primary` `#0d9488`).
- Reuse existing CSS variables and UI primitives (`bg-background`, `bg-primary`, `bg-card`, `border-border`, `Button`/`Card`/`Badge`).
- Preserve logo (`BrandLogo` / syncvete-logo), DM Sans + Fraunces, and light/dark via `.dark` + `data-accent`.
- Improve layout, spacing, navigation, cards, tables, and interactions without changing the brand palette.
- Treat MyVete only as a reference for workflow organization / operational UX — never for colors, logo, or type.

## Must not

- Do not adopt MyVete’s purple scheme as the SyncVete look (no hardcoded `#7c3aed` / `#8b5cf6` / purple-on-white themes as UI V2 defaults).
- Do not invent a second purple stylesheet for clinic staff UI.
- Do not change `DEFAULT_THEME.accent` away from `teal`.
- Do not replace SyncVete logo or display/sans font identity.

## Allowed exceptions

- User-selected accent presets in `COLOR_PRESETS` (including optional violet) remain user preference, not product branding.
- Owner portal neon / clinic `primaryColor` white-label is out of scope for clinic staff brand rules.

## When touching clinic UI

Prefer token classes over new hex colors. If a status color is needed, reuse dashboard tones (teal/sky/emerald/amber/rose/cyan) already in the codebase.
